variants.how:
P0 opaque canvas plus P1 honest foliage applied to the existing proxy models. It shows how much of 'not real enough' was the renderer.

Shared render fixes, applied identically to EVERY variant:
- alpha:false (opaque canvas);
- foliage shader v2: translucency injected before totalDiffuse, roughness 0.5-0.85, no back-face normal flip, crown normals, AO-gated;
- no albedo lift or green gain;
- coverage-preserving alpha mips;
- a shadow customDepthMaterial at the visible alpha cutoff;
- a minimal bed-seating stub on the demo bed (mulch level fix and contact decal);
- idle 8-16-frame accumulation;
- Photo mode with the emissive leaf glow removed, thin-wall transmission 0.1-0.25 at roughness about 0.6, transmissiveBounces 12 and sun radius 0.265 deg.

Prototype the plan's builders for the three species only:
- P3 hull-plus-shell for 'Smaragd';
- P5 shrub with baked globe heads for Annabelle;
- P7 space-colonisation tree for sugar maple.
Each gets LOD0 at the plan cap (clipped evergreen 3k, shrub 3.5k, tree 12k triangles) plus a raised stills-only LOD0 (about 12k / 15k / 60k) to test whether triangles buy realism. LOD1 and the LOD2 billboard cloud follow the plan. Shared atlases, and the same per-instance variation turned off so every variant is compared like for like.

Buy single-species packs:
- Maxtree V122_Thuja_occidentalis_01 (reshaped toward a 'Smaragd' habit), or the exact-cultivar Superhive 'Thuja Smaragd Collection vol 138' (US$7);
- a Maxtree Acer saccharum single-species pack;
- a Maxtree Hydrangea macrophylla pack, with heads recoloured white as the Annabelle stand-in.
In Blender 5.2: decimate to the same caps as V1, bake 1-2k leaf and bark atlases, and build LOD1 and an LOD2 billboard cloud with the shared shader. Files live in a folder OUTSIDE the repo and are never committed, deployed or put on a public URL. Phone testing goes only through the plan's LAN probe server. Maxtree EULA s.2.1(1) permits private use and modification.

bakeoff.cameras_and_modes:
The P0 fixture (31-plant demo bed plus lawn trees), with each variant swapped in by species id at render time; no saved data changes.

CAMERAS:
- Corner;
- Front;
- Bed close-up (eye 60 in, 120 in from the bed centre, aimed at 18 in, fov 38);
- Bed edge low (eye 30 in);
- Plant base macro (for the shrub);
- Tree in lawn (eye about 30 in, about 5 ft from the maple);
- Overview, for context.
The 273-plant estate at Corner is used only for the perf check of the winning variant.

LIVE VIEW, per variant, in Day and Golden hour with Realistic look on:
- desktop 1600x900 at forced high tier (MSAA 4, LOD0/LOD1, 4096 shadows, PCSS);
- phone 390x844 at forced balanced (LOD1, MSAA 2, DPR 1.25);
- phone 390x844 at forced constrained (LOD2, no MSAA, no plant shadows).
Each is captured as a still after idle accumulation AND as a 10 s orbit clip, because shimmer and LOD pops while orbiting are judged by eye. The owner also opens every variant on his iPhone in portrait through the LAN probe server (balanced tier) and records p50/p95 frame times and context loss.

SHOWCASE STILL EXPORT: forced LOD0 at both the plan cap and the raised stills cap.

PHOTO MODE: the WebGL tracer with the leaf-transmission fixes, 384 spp plus denoise, at Corner, Front, Bed close-up and Tree in lawn, Day and Golden hour.

METRICS from the P0 probe, per variant and tier:
- triangles and draws per pass;
- plant texture MiB;
- p95 frame time;
- overdraw at Front and Bed close-up;
- canopy luminance and % of pixels above sRGB 235;
- ColorChecker ΔE2000 of the mean sunlit-leaf colour against the owner's calibrated reference photo.

bakeoff.judge:
The owner, by eye, in a blind session. For each species × camera × tier/mode, a contact sheet shows the variants under randomised letters, beside the owner's REAL reference photo taken from the matching viewpoint. The owner marks each tile 'real enough / not', ranks them, and plays the orbit clips side by side.

Optional second gate: 5-10 homeowners (staff, clients, friends; recruiting them is the owner's outreach) get 10 render/photo crop pairs at Corner and Front from Photo mode and the desktop still, and say which is the photo. Target: no better than 60% correct identification.

Objective guardrails reported alongside:
- ΔE2000 of about 5 or less against calibrated photos;
- silhouette porosity within ±10% of the reference at equal pixel height;
- no shimmer after 8+ accumulated samples;
- p95 at most 1.15× P0 on balanced and constrained;
- constrained tier under 45k triangles;
- texture MiB within the tier budgets.

DECISION RULE:
- If V2 is 'real enough' in Photo mode and the desktop still at Corner and Front, and is not visibly worse than V3 on phones, adopt route 2 for all 26 and skip paid assets.
- If V3 or V4 clearly beat V2 while V1/V2 fail, the gap is geometry. Next steps are a PlantFactory or commission pilot for trees, and only then Maxtree licence confirmation.
- If every variant fails on phones but passes in Photo mode, accept the phone ceiling and invest in Photo mode (WebGPU tracer, then optionally server-side Cycles), not assets.

rendering_upgrades:
Foliage shader v2, injected at <aomap_fragment> before totalDiffuse (today's translucency, warm-highlight and shade-fill terms are added after outgoingLight is summed, so they never render). Contents:
- a diffuse-transmission lobe T·albedo_t·max(0,-N·L)·shadow/π plus a small irradiance term from -N, scaled by baked thickness and AO, and multiplied by the sun shadow so beds do not go neon;
- upper-side roughness 0.5-0.65 and under-side 0.7-0.85, F0 0.04;
- no back-face normal flip for leaf cards;
- crown or proxy-sphere normals blended 50-80% into the card normals;
- a per-vertex AO attribute driving specular occlusion;
- Toksvig or geometric specular AA;
- removal of the pow(0.8) albedo lift and the green gain.
About 1-1.5 KB gzip in the lazy Landscape3D chunk and 2 B/vertex. GPU estimate +0.1-0.3 ms desktop, +0.3-1 ms phone. Mirror every change in photoMaterials.ts so the live view and Photo mode agree.

Alpha pipeline:
- coverage-preserving mips baked offline (Castaño bisection per mip) so maple canopies do not blob and needle atlases do not vanish at distance;
- an optional mip-level alpha scale (about 4 ALU ops);
- a customDepthMaterial at the visible cutoff for plant shadows (three forces alphaTest 0.5 for A2C in WebGLShadowMap.js:482, against the visible 0.3-0.4);
- alphaHash on the constrained tier only, and only together with accumulation.

Shadows and grounding:
- PCSS sized to the real 0.53 deg sun (penumbra about 0.0093 × occluder distance) on the high and showcase tiers only (+0.3-1 ms desktop);
- Photo-mode sun radius 0.265 deg in place of 0.9 deg (photoGrade.ts:26), so penumbrae and sun flecks are not 3.4x too soft;
- an instanced radial contact decal under every plant on all tiers (constrained phones have no plant shadows; about 0.05 ms);
- the GroundOcclusion texture fed to bed materials;
- per-vertex canopy AO on top of GTAO.
Shadow texel size (150 ft frustum): 0.44 in at 4096, 0.88 in at 2048, 1.76 in at 1024. Leaf-scale dapple is therefore plausible only on high and showcase.

Colour calibration and grade:
- ColorChecker-referenced RAW photos per species, with a virtual ColorChecker in the scene;
- per-species mean sunlit-leaf ΔE2000 of about 5 or less, and 2-4 ΔE variation per plant;
- summer foliage linear albedo about 0.09-0.12;
- a phone-camera-like curve (S-curve plus highlight roll-off) for Realistic look and Photo mode, with Neutral kept for editor swatches;
- the Neutral (live) versus AgX (Photo mode) green divergence resolved.

Geometry and density policy:
- true-size twig-cluster cards (shrub cards are about 12x real leaf size today);
- species crown envelopes with real porosity (10-30% sky gaps for deciduous crowns, about 0 for clipped evergreens);
- opaque leaf meshes for hosta, daylily, grasses and hero flower heads;
- uniform or XZ-isotropic scaling;
- LOD1 enlarges the retained cards by sqrt(1/retention);
- LOD2 as a billboard cloud or a hemi-octahedral impostor with baked normals and depth (agargaro/octahedral-impostor, MIT), so it relights with the sun;
- per-instance variation plus 2 seeded variants (D22).

Photo mode on the current WebGLPathTracer (three-gpu-pathtracer 0.0.27):
- drop the shadow-unaware emissive leaf glow and the albedo lift (photoMaterials.ts:183-189, 422-436);
- thin-wall transmission 0.1-0.25 at roughness about 0.6, or better a roughly 50-line GLSL Lambertian transmission lobe applied only to thin-film, rough transmissive materials so glass stays specular;
- transmissiveBounces 10-16 (alpha skips starve shadow rays and over-darken canopies);
- sun radius 0.265 deg;
- textureSize 2048 only for close-up stills (16 MB per layer, applies to every scene texture);
- baked LOD0 limited to plants in or near the frustum.
Pin 0.0.27, because the WebGL tracer was deprecated in 0.0.25.

